# 16. FUNCTIONAL ACCEPTANCE SCENARIOS

The demonstration is successful only if the following flows work end-to-end:

### Scenario 1 — Employee and organization

Create a synthetic employee, assign them to a sector and position, and verify that the same employee appears in both ORGANIZACIÓN and PERSONAL.

### Scenario 2 — Daily staffing

Assign the employee to a shift, record an absence and verify that the staffing view and employee history both reflect the change.

### Scenario 3 — Checklist with traceability

Assign a procedure, complete its checklist, register the performing employee and submitting user, then verify or dispute the result from an authorized supervisor role.

The history must show the relevant actors and timestamps.

### Scenario 4 — Purchase cycle

Create a purchase request, verify stock, adjust quantities, approve the purchase, generate a PDF order and record a receipt.

All steps must refer to the same underlying request and preserve their history.

### Scenario 5 — Waste and inventory

Register 3 kg of spoiled shrimp as waste, link it to the appropriate inventory adjustment and verify that the waste analytics and stock quantities are consistent.

### Scenario 6 — Yield loss

Record 2 kg gross input and 1.7 kg usable output.

Verify:
- Loss: 0.3 kg.
- Loss percentage: 15%.
- Yield: 85%.

Do not calculate monetary impact without a known cost.

### Scenario 7 — Employee lifecycle

Record a position transfer and verify that the current assignment changes while the previous assignment remains in the historical timeline.

### Scenario 8 — Financial import

Import a compatible synthetic CSV, map columns, preview records, confirm the import and verify that the corresponding dashboard indicators update.

Reimporting the same file should not silently duplicate records.

### Scenario 9 — Payroll preparation

Record an approved advance, associate it with an employee and verify that the payroll preparation view shows the authorized adjustment without automatically executing a payment.

### Scenario 10 — Persistence

Refresh the application and verify that changes made during the demonstration remain available in the same browser environment.

